 of 12 are 1, 2, 3, 4, 6 and 12.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Find all the factors of 36.","steps":["Pairs: 1 × 36, 2 × 18, 3 × 12, 4 × 9 and 6 × 6. (5 does not divide 36.)","After 6 × 6 the pairs repeat, so stop.","Factors of 36: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, 18, 36."]},"watch":"1 and the number itself are always factors. Do not forget them.","qs":[{"text":"How many different rectangles can you make with 16 squares? (A 2 × 8 and an 8 × 2 rectangle count as one.)","vis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:208px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 60\"><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"45.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"75.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"90.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"105.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"120.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"135.0\" y=\"6.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"30.0\" y=\"21.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"45.0\" y=\"21.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"21.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"75.0\" y=\"21.0\" width=\"15.0\" height=\"15.0\" fill=\"#E3D6CE\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><